            "description": "Specifies a subdomain that can be used to receive Inbound calls to a Connection, in the same way a phone number is used, from a SIP endpoint. Example: the subdomain \"example.sip.telnyx.com\" can be called from any SIP endpoint by using the SIP URI \"sip:@example.sip.telnyx.com\" where the user part can be any alphanumeric value. TLS signaling is supported. SRTP media encryption requires TLS transport.",
